{"slug": "volume5-part1/284", "title": "30-D.", "volume": "volume5-part1", "sourceUrl": "https://budget.up.nic.in/Fin_H_Book/volume5/part1/284.html", "html": "<font color=\"#000080\" size=\"5\"><p align=\"CENTER\">FORM No. 30-D</p>\n<p align=\"CENTER\">(See Chapter XIII, paragraph 307)</p>\n<p align=\"CENTER\">NOTES</p>\n<p align=\"CENTER\">COMPARATIVE STATEMENT OF TENDERS</p>\n</font><font color=\"#800000\" size=\"4\"><p align=\"JUSTIFY\">On the line set apart for ‘contractor’s qualifications’, in this form it will suffice simply to enter any of the letters (a), (b), (c) according to the following qualifications :</p>\n<p align=\"JUSTIFY\">(a) The contractor’s name is not in the circle black book.</p>\n<p align=\"JUSTIFY\">(b) The contractor has carried out three works each amounting to Rs. 20,000 or more.</p>\n<p align=\"JUSTIFY\">(c) The contractor has carried out three works each amounting to Rs. 2,000 or more.</p></font>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"7\" cellspacing=\"0\" width=\"641\">\n<tr><td valign=\"TOP\" width=\"50%\">\n<font color=\"#800000\" size=\"4\"><p align=\"JUSTIFY\">2. If contracts are tendered for in detail for each item of work the items will be entered in column 1, but if tenders are for a percentage below estimated rate, details need not be given.</p></font></td>\n<td valign=\"BOTTOM\" width=\"50%\">\n<font color=\"#800000\" size=\"4\"><p align=\"JUSTIFY\">Rank,</p></font></td>\n</tr>\n<tr><td height=\"269\" valign=\"TOP\" width=\"50%\"><p></p></td>\n<td height=\"269\" valign=\"TOP\" width=\"50%\">\n<font color=\"#800000\" size=\"4\"><p align=\"JUSTIFY\">—————District.</p></font></td>\n</tr>\n<tr><td valign=\"TOP\" width=\"50%\"> </td>\n<td valign=\"TOP\" width=\"50%\">\n<font color=\"#800000\" size=\"4\"><p align=\"JUSTIFY\">Rank,</p></font></td>\n</tr>\n<tr><td valign=\"TOP\" width=\"50%\"> </td>\n<td valign=\"TOP\" width=\"50%\">\n<font color=\"#800000\" size=\"4\"><p align=\"JUSTIFY\">—————District.</p></font></td>\n</tr>\n</table>\n